      },
      "lineNbr": 22,
      "author": {
        "id": 1291807
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-05-08T21:14:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The \"or\" part of this is counter-intuitive to me.  Is there a reason for not requiring vid+pid match when they are given alongside serial number?  I don\u0027t see how there can be a guarantee of serial number uniqueness across different vid:pid.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 20,
        "startChar": 36,
        "endLine": 22,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "26c1ba556c089d4bf16454cf634a07a54ca36981",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "75c51ba1_0d7e238c",
        "filename": "util/usb_if.h",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 22,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-05-08T21:26:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think we should require the user to pass in vid/pid along with serial number on the command line.\n\nThe likelihood of having two different devices having the same serial number is extremely low and could be neglected IMO.",
      "parentUuid": "620b42b5_752ca670",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 20,
        "startChar": 36,
        "endLine": 22,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "26c1ba556c089d4bf16454cf634a07a54ca36981",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8d3bb753_9aead41a",
        "filename": "util/usb_if.h",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 22,
      "author": {
        "id": 1291807
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-05-08T21:38:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I wouldn\u0027t require vid:pid alongside serialno.  I am saying if vid:pid are given, to respect them.",
      "parentUuid": "75c51ba1_0d7e238c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 20,
        "startChar": 36,
        "endLine": 22,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "26c1ba556c089d4bf16454cf634a07a54ca36981",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "39346819_3af0a73c",
        "filename": "util/usb_if.h",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 22,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-05-08T21:41:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this (allowing to give vid/pid along with sn) would complicate processing logic for no particularly good reason.\n\nHow about we should start without it and then add it if a need arises.",
      "parentUuid": "8d3bb753_9aead41a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 20,
        "startChar": 36,
        "endLine": 22,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "26c1ba556c089d4bf16454cf634a07a54ca36981",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "01ad109a_152ce85e",
        "filename": "util/usb_if.h",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 22,
      "author": {
        "id": 1136059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-05-08T21:42:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The issue is iteflash and gsctool default to non-zero vid pid. So to use those scripts we have to give the vid pid and serialnumber of the device to override those defaults.\n\nWe can change those scripts so the default vid pid is 0 if the user gives a serial number.",
      "parentUuid": "8d3bb753_9aead41a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 20,
        "startChar": 36,
        "endLine": 22,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "26c1ba556c089d4bf16454cf634a07a54ca36981",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8b6962b7_7e02e287",
        "filename": "util/usb_if.h",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 22,
      "author": {
        "id": 1291807
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-05-08T21:46:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Just make sure the help output shows default values.  No need to change default vid:pid based on serialno being given.\n\nI think most of the time the user won\u0027t need to override them anyways even when giving a serial number.",
      "parentUuid": "01ad109a_152ce85e",
      "range": {
